<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81356" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιηγ-έομαι</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιᾱγ-</span></b> , fut.
			-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ήσομαι</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Men.
			<u>Her.Fr.</u>
			9
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lead
			round</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὸ ὄρος τοῖσι Πέρσῃσι</span>
			<i>show</i> them <i>the way round</i> the mountain, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.214
			</span></i> : abs., <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(1).689
			</span></i>(Corc.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Delph.</u>
				3(1).362i16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs.,
				<i>explain, describe</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Cont.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, <i>D Mort.</i><i><span class="en">
				20.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be made to revolve</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philol.
				[21]
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>draw in outline, describe in general terms</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμπληροῦν τὸ περιηγηθέν</span> (used in
			pass. sense), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				770b
			</span></i>.— 
				Act.
			 only <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιήγει:
			ἐζωγράφει</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
